{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most of the 30-day horizon, with the underestimation growing as the realized uptrend strengthens.",
    "Trend/level lag: the model behaves mean-reverting around the recent history level while the true series trends upward; it fails to follow regime shifts quickly (needs a positive drift term when recent returns turn positive).",
    "Horizon-dependent error: underprediction is small in the first ~1–5 days but widens materially from ~day 7 onward; apply an increasing upward adjustment with forecast horizon (e.g., ramped additive bias).",
    "Upside convexity miss: during sustained rallies the model’s amplitude is too muted (it predicts sideways/soft pullbacks while outcomes keep rising); scale up positive moves when short-term momentum is positive.",
    "Breakout underreaction: after a local low in history, the model does not lift the path enough; when the last 5–10 days show a rebound, shift the entire forecast distribution upward rather than reverting to the prior mean."
  ]
}
